  "notes": "{堤防|ていぼう} refers to man-made structures for flood prevention, built along rivers, coasts, or lakes.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {堤防|ていぼう}が{決壊|けっかい}する: the levee breaks\n- {堤防|ていぼう}を{築|きず}く: to build an embankment\n- {堤防|ていぼう}を{強化|きょうか}する: to reinforce an embankment\n- {堤防|ていぼう}{沿|ぞ}い: along the embankment\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {防波堤|ぼうはてい}: breakwater (sea wall)\n- {土手|どて}: embankment, bank (more casual, often grassy)",
